# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Training-set sizes and the energy and force errors of the coupled-cluster models are in Supplementary Table 2, not in the PDF read ('a few hundred molecular conformations'); no numConfigurations and no AccuracyMetric are encoded. The main text gives only that sGDML reaches a force MAE of 1 kcal/mol/A with about 200 training examples on DFT data (GDML: about 800).
# - The DFT-trained sGDML and GDML models for ten molecules (benzene to azobenzene, Fig. 2 and Table I) are not encoded as runs; the PBE+TS reference calculation is declared for the sampling level and is not attached to a data set.
# - mlips:CCSDT is used for CCSD(T), as in smith2019ccx (DLPNO_CCSDT); the vocabulary has no separate individual for full CCSDT, so this reading should be confirmed.
# - Classical and path-integral MD (i-PI, 16 beads, 0.2 fs) with the sGDML models are demonstrated; the spectroscopic and conformational results have no MetricProperty.
# - The manifest classes this paper as 'Application/model instance'; it is the originating sGDML method paper (registry origin of entity:sGDML).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
